m).** It is written in `.theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-web-apps-documenteditor.md`. Round 1's condition was that this module's share of the time before the document is requested be over 200 ms. It is about 0.9 s of the roughly 1.1 s of busy time before the editor asks for the document, and round 2 measured the same split again. The toolbar build and the Comments startup are the biggest single items.\n\n**What round 1 did and did not deliver:** it produced measurements and two oracles but changed no code, so it made nothing faster. The original and new web-apps are the same commit (`d238e526`). That means the differential oracle passes on all 4 cases but only shows noise: up to ±0.7 s per open on identical code.\n\n**Round 2 numbers**, in `.theseus/oracle/rounds/web-apps-documenteditor-r2.md`:\n- The document is requested 1.20–1.25 s after the page starts loading, and is ready at 3.3–3.9 s.\n- Busy time before that request:\n\n| Part | ms |\n|---|---|\n| jQuery and other vendor files | 386–414 |\n| documenteditor's own code | 148–152 |\n| apps/common code | 150–166 |\n| Script parse and compile | 171–220 |\n| sdkjs | 68–72 |\n\n**Next-round plan** (all JavaScript, in `external/web-apps`):\n- **P1:** build the toolbar tabs that are not shown until they are first opened.\n- **P2:** move the Comments build to after the document has loaded.\n- **P3 (wave 1):** cut the caption width measuring in `Button.js`, if the toolbar still costs more than 150 ms after P1.\n\nEach must pass both oracles. It also needs a before/after of `perf/open-window.js` over 5 runs, because single runs are too noisy. If P1 and P2 together gain less than 150 ms, the verdict becomes keep. If an earlier document request does not make the document ready sooner, the work moves to sdkjs.\n\n**Other:** there was no `-b` diagnosis to delete. The executor log is filled in and the friction line is appended. No source code changed.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- A round that only measures delivers no speed. Once its condition is met, the next round must plan code changes.\n- On this 2-CPU VM, a gain under about 0.5 s only shows up over repeated `open-window.js` runs, not in the differential oracle's single-run timings.","ttft_ms":3570,"type":"result","duration_ms":383024,"uuid":"34614ca3-d7fa-4a58-a0d2-78cafc177f97","ttft_stream_ms":2251,"time_to_request_ms":501,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":354,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":24,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":8,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":31,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":13,"request_build":9},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":143,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":278,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":210,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":138,"process_rss_mib_result":232,"process_anon_mib_result":143,"process_peak_rss_mib":267,"process_cpu_ms_turn":5295,"process_wall_ms_turn":383023,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1592,"process_wall_ms_streaming":80583,"main_stream_count":14,"main_stream_event_count":1620,"main_stream_chunk_count":1078,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":1592,"wall_ms":80583,"entries":14},"tool":{"cpu_ms":2461,"wall_ms":261958,"entries":13},"first_event_wait":{"cpu_ms":590,"wall_ms":39625,"entries":14},"before_first_request":{"cpu_ms":278,"wall_ms":501,"entries":1},"between_requests":{"cpu_ms":357,"wall_ms":339,"entries":13},"after_last_request":{"cpu_ms":17,"wall_ms":17,"entries":1}},"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":8,"cpu_ms":26,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":1,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":11,"ambient_wait_ms":8,"render_ms":2,"producers":41,"to